## Decisions

### Before you restart the PDF page catch-up, can I change the uploader so it waits out server restarts instead of exiting?

**What this is:** the PDF page catch-up is `go run ./tools/pdfthumbnails`, the laptop tool that renders every page of each PDF document, uploads the page images, waits for the server to thumbnail them, then copies the first page's thumbnail onto the PDF. It stopped last night. **854 PDF documents** on production still lack complete pages or a thumbnail. At last night's pace (~25 PDFs an hour, mostly spent waiting for each write to reach the sheet) that's roughly 1½ days of running.

**Deploy: nothing to ask.** The workload-isolation change (shared CPU budget, foreground priority) is already live. Cloud Build deployed it when the merge was pushed, and revision `heliosian-01102-22l` has served it since 18:32 UTC today.

**Why the tool stopped three times last night.** Each time the trigger was production's routine instance replacement, not upload load. Cloud Run swaps the single instance several times a day even with nothing running: today at 11:00, 11:09, 11:12, 12:38, 14:11 and 14:15 UTC, each time while the old instance was idle (CPU 0, heap ~900 MiB). A new instance spends ~60s loading before it listens. Requests in that window fail. It also re-tries 5 old, permanently broken thumbnails (two images over the pixel limit, two campaugusta.org 503s, one `localhost:3000` image). Those count as "thumbnails pending" for ~10 minutes, three tries 5 minutes apart.

Real log lines from last night, and what each version of the tool does with them:

| What happened | Today's tool | Proposed tool |
|---|---|---|
| `ERROR draw pdfs error="send pdf docA6jJkVzIdDj: processing did not drain within five minutes: thumbnails=5"` (the 5 broken thumbnails after a restart) | exits; someone restarts it by hand | keeps waiting, logging `waiting for processing pending="thumbnails=5"` once a minute, and continues when the third try clears them (~10 min) |
| `/api/queues` answered 500, and `/api/do/pdf-page` answered 502 twice, while a new instance started (05:56, 05:57, 06:09 UTC) | retries 3 times over ~65s, then exits | logs `server unavailable, starting over in=30s`, waits 30s, rereads which PDFs are still incomplete, and resumes. Pages already stored are re-sent; the server answers success for identical bytes and adds no duplicate |
| `429` | exits | exits (unchanged; nothing on these endpoints sends one) |
| `400` for one document (its PDF changed meanwhile) | skips that document | skips that document (unchanged) |

**What stays the same:** it still waits after every page and every write until thumbnails, search indexing, search processing and pending writes are all at 0. Which PDFs still need work is still read from real completion state (`rendered` set and `thumbnail` set). Identical PDFs still reuse a completed copy's page images and thumbnail.

**Also updated:** the `AGENTS.md` line telling agents not to resume a run stopped by overload without checking health, and the `docs/dev.md` line saying a queue stuck five minutes stops the run. Both would describe the new behavior instead.

- (*) Make it wait out restarts
  Make the change above, test it, then hand you the command. Under the hood, the uploader's own 3-try retry is replaced by one 30-second "start the pass over" loop around the whole run. You'd watch it in a terminal; a real stuck queue shows up as the same `waiting for processing` line repeating every minute.
- ( ) Run it as it is
  No code change. I hand you the command now. Expect it to exit after most instance replacements (several a day), and to need restarting by hand each time.

